**********************************************************************
** MMP0400 - QUALITY INSPECTION HOLD                                **
** New (2026-09) manufacturing scenario: an inspector places a mill  **
** order on quality hold. Shares MILL-ORDER with MMP0100 and calls   **
** the same MMN0900 audit routine, so the two programs' call graphs  **
** and data-flow connect through both. Records the hold against the  **
** new QUALITY-HOLD entity, entered via the MMM0150 map.             **
**********************************************************************
DEFINE DATA
PARAMETER
1 #ORDER-NO          (A10)
1 #RETURN-CODE       (N2)
LOCAL
1 ORDER-VIEW VIEW OF MILL-ORDER
  2 ORDER-NO
  2 ORDER-STATUS
1 HOLD-VIEW VIEW OF QUALITY-HOLD
  2 ORDER-NO
  2 HOLD-REASON
  2 HOLD-DATE
  2 INSPECTOR-ID
  2 HOLD-STATUS
1 #HOLD-REASON       (A30)
1 #INSPECTOR-ID      (A8)
1 #TODAY             (D) INIT <*DATX>
END-DEFINE
*
RESET #RETURN-CODE
*
INPUT USING MAP 'MMM0150'
*
F1. FIND ORDER-VIEW WITH ORDER-NO = #ORDER-NO
  IF NO RECORDS FOUND
    MOVE 40 TO #RETURN-CODE
    ESCAPE ROUTINE
  END-NOREC
  REJECT IF ORDER-VIEW.ORDER-STATUS = 'HELD'
  MOVE 'HELD' TO ORDER-VIEW.ORDER-STATUS
  UPDATE(F1.)
END-FIND
*
MOVE #ORDER-NO TO HOLD-VIEW.ORDER-NO
MOVE #HOLD-REASON TO HOLD-VIEW.HOLD-REASON
MOVE #TODAY TO HOLD-VIEW.HOLD-DATE
MOVE #INSPECTOR-ID TO HOLD-VIEW.INSPECTOR-ID
MOVE 'OPEN' TO HOLD-VIEW.HOLD-STATUS
STORE HOLD-VIEW
END TRANSACTION
*
CALLNAT 'MMN0900' #ORDER-NO
*
END
